1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,380
What if saving someone you love is

2
00:00:02,390 --> 00:00:04,680
the very act that leaves you alone?

3
00:00:05,320 --> 00:00:06,180
In Greek myth,

4
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:09,750
Ariadne, daughter of King Minos of Crete,

5
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:14,580
sees the Athenian prince Theseus among youths

6
00:00:14,590 --> 00:00:16,160
condemned to enter the Labyrinth.

7
00:00:18,540 --> 00:00:20,300
He intends to face the Minotaur,

8
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:21,920
a bull-headed monster.

9
00:00:21,930 --> 00:00:22,460
No one expects him to return.

10
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:26,340
Ariadne gives Theseus a sword and a

11
00:00:26,350 --> 00:00:27,540
spool of red thread.

12
00:00:27,550 --> 00:00:29,360
At the maze entrance,

13
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:32,020
she ties one end to the stone

14
00:00:32,030 --> 00:00:34,760
and makes him promise to unwind it

15
00:00:34,770 --> 00:00:37,420
behind him. The blade may kill the

16
00:00:37,430 --> 00:00:40,240
monster; only the thread can bring him

17
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:40,674
back.

18
00:00:41,660 --> 00:00:45,100
Theseus follows the thread into darkness and

19
00:00:45,110 --> 00:00:46,200
finds the Minotaur.

20
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:48,460
Their fight shakes the maze.

21
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:50,480
When the creature falls,

22
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:53,640
Theseus grips the red line and follows

23
00:00:53,650 --> 00:00:54,640
it toward daylight,

24
00:00:55,120 --> 00:00:57,449
while those outside wait for a sound.

25
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:01,600
Ariadne abandons her father and sails with

26
00:01:01,610 --> 00:01:04,200
Theseus into the open Aegean.

27
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:06,060
Crete sinks behind them.

28
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:08,020
She has risked her home,

29
00:01:08,280 --> 00:01:10,740
her name, and everything she owns,

30
00:01:11,280 --> 00:01:13,460
but on the deck she lets herself

31
00:01:13,470 --> 00:01:15,608
believe he will not abandon her.

32
00:01:16,660 --> 00:01:20,420
At Naxos, the ship leaves Ariadne sleeping

33
00:01:20,430 --> 00:01:21,240
on the shore.

34
00:01:21,960 --> 00:01:23,200
She wakes to waves,

35
00:01:23,820 --> 00:01:25,140
searches empty sand,

36
00:01:25,420 --> 00:01:29,200
and sees Theseus's sail shrinking beyond reach.

37
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:30,980
In that instant,

38
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:33,170
rescue becomes betrayal.

39
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:38,040
Ancient tellings disagree about Ariadne's fate.

40
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:39,860
But the image endures:

41
00:01:40,460 --> 00:01:42,320
the woman who led a hero out

42
00:01:42,330 --> 00:01:44,580
of death is left without a home.

43
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:46,040
On the shore,

44
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:48,940
Ariadne holds one end of the red

45
00:01:48,950 --> 00:01:52,020
thread. Nothing answers from the other side.
